## Why This Is Asked

Probes ability to implement a practical, end-to-end beginner pipeline with drift checks and lineage.

## Key Concepts

- Data Factory pipelines and Data Flows
- Drift validation against expected schema
- Spark MERGE upserts in Synapse
- Purview lineage tagging
- Checkpointing and late arrival handling

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo drift check
function hasDrift(actualSchema, expected) {
  const a = new Set(actualSchema);
  const b = new Set(expected);
  return a.size !== b.size || [...a].some(col => !b.has(col));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle reprocessing of failed files without duplicating rows?
- How would you validate drift in a streaming window vs daily batch?

## Why This Is Asked

This angle tests ability to handle schema drift with a metadata-driven approach, using config files to map columns rather than code changes, plus basic lineage and idempotent loading.

## Key Concepts

- Config-driven schema mapping
- Mapping Data Flows in Data Factory
- Upserts with MERGE into Synapse
- Purview lineage and data quality gating

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example config structure
const config = {
  partners: {
    PartnerA: { srcCols: ["date","sales"], tgtCols: ["Date","Amount"] },
    PartnerB: { srcCols: ["sale_date","value"], tgtCols: ["Date","Amount"] }
  }
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test changing the config for a new partner?
- How would you handle a sudden drop of a required column?
